0	141	Martin Bangemann (15 November 1934 – 28 June 2022) was a German politician and a leader of the Free Democratic Party (FDP) from 1985 to 1988.
142	225	He was German Federal Minister for Economic Affairs and a European Commissioner.



225	294	Life and career

Bangemann was born on 15 November 1934 in Wanzleben.
295	355	He studied law in Tübingen and Munich, and earned a Dr. jur.
356	536	(not equivalent to J.D., but a PhD in law) in 1962 with a dissertation entitled Bilder und Fiktionen in Recht und Rechtswissenschaft (Imagery and fiction in law and jurisprudence).
537	573	He qualified as an attorney in 1964.
574	601	In 1963, he joined the FDP.
602	646	He worked as a lawyer in Baden-Württemberg.

646	733	In 1972, he was elected to the Bundestag and briefly was Secretary General of the FDP.

733	905	Bangemann was a member of the European Parliament from 1973 to 1984; from 1976 to 1979 he was vice-chairman, from 1979 to 1984 chairman of the Liberal and Democratic Group.
906	971	From 1978 to 1979 he was vice-chair of the Committee on Budgets.

971	1052	Bangemann was the German Federal Minister for Economic Affairs from 1984 to 1988.
1053	1152	'During his tenure, he had to deal with high unemployment and the steel, coal and shipyard crises.

1152	1202	In 1988, Bangemann joined the European Commission.
1203	1313	He was Commissioner for the Internal Market and Industrial Affairs in the Delors Commission from 1989 to 1995.
1314	1465	Subsequently, he became Commissioner for Industrial affairs, Information & Telecommunications Technologies in the Santer Commission from 1995 to 1999.

1465	1586	As commissioner, he led a "high-level group" that drew up the report "Europe and the Global Information Society" in 1994.
1587	1724	This document contained recommendations to the European Council on measures that Europe should take regarding information infrastructure.
1725	1800	It became known as the "Bangemann report" and influenced many EU policies.

1800	1882	He then moved from European politics to the board of the Spanish group Telefónica.
1883	1931	In addition, Bangemann ran a consulting agency.

1931	1969	He was married and had five children.

1969	2067	Bangemann died from a heart attack at his home in Deux-Sèvres on 28 June 2022 at the age of 87.



